# MedievalZen - git attributes
#
# Binary assets go through Git LFS. Install Git LFS and run `git lfs install` once per machine
# before cloning; in a clone made without it, run `git lfs pull` (Tools/AssetCheck reports
# pointer files that were never fetched). Unity's text formats (.unity, .prefab, .asset, .mat,
# .meta, .controller, .anim, .terrainlayer, ...) stay in plain git so they diff and merge.
#
# The third-party packs (Assets/Synty, Assets/polyperfect, Assets/Sounds) are not in the
# repository at all: see .gitignore and Tools/AssetCheck/third-party-packs.txt.

# Scripts keep the line endings their interpreter needs
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.cs    diff=csharp

# --- Git LFS: images ---
*.png   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
